# What must not reach the build context.
#
# `node_modules` is the one that matters. The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` before
# copying the source, so a host `node_modules` copied over the top replaces
# the container's workspace symlinks with Windows-built binaries — and the
# build then fails to resolve `@drainlens/schema`, which reads like a missing
# dependency rather than the overwrite it is.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Rebuilt inside the image; copying it in risks publishing
# something older than the source beside it.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# The Python side is never deployed.
pipeline/.venv
**/__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.coverage

# Full-size intermediates, including a 4 GB point cloud. The published
# artefacts under apps/web/public/data are committed and must NOT be ignored.
/data

.git
.github
.idea
.claude
coverage
